Usage: mcpdo [options] [command]

MCP Inspector connection CLI — connect once, run many commands against a named
connection.

Agent skill for mcpdo: install with `npx skills add
modelcontextprotocol/inspector --skill mcpdo`, or see `agent-help` below.

Options:
  --version                                                  output the version number
  --format <format>                                          Output format: text (default; human-readable) or json (pretty-printed)
  --plain                                                    Disable ANSI styling (color, bold/dim, hyperlinks) in human text output
  --connection <name>                                        Connection name (without required @). Overrides MRU / positional @name. `--conn` is a supported shorthand.
  --catalog <path>                                           Writable catalog file (default: ~/.mcp-inspector/mcp.json or MCP_CATALOG_PATH)
  --config <path>                                            Read-only connection config file (never written or seeded)
  --stored-auth-only                                         Never start interactive OAuth; use the shared store if present, otherwise fail.
  -h, --help                                                 Display help for command

Commands:
  servers/list                                               List catalog/config server entries (marks live connections when the daemon is running; no MCP connection)
  servers/show [name]                                        Show one catalog/config entry in detail (no MCP connection; secrets redacted)
  connect [options] [target...]                              Connect a catalog entry or ad-hoc target as a named connection
  disconnect [options] [connection]                          Disconnect a connection (MRU when omitted on a TTY)
  connections/list                                           List open connections (marks MRU); does not start the daemon
  connections/use <connection>                               Set the MRU connection without an MCP RPC
  connections/show [connection]                              Show connection + connection details: server info, capabilities, negotiated protocol era (defaults to MRU)
  auth/list                                                  List servers in the shared OAuth store, annotated with catalog/connection names
  auth/clear [options] [key]                                 Clear stored OAuth state for one server (URL or catalog/connection name from auth/list) or all entries
  auth/ema-status                                            Show enterprise-managed auth (EMA) configuration and IdP login state
  auth/ema-login [options]                                   Sign in to the enterprise IdP (EMA); subsequent connects to EMA servers mint tokens silently from this connection
  auth/ema-logout                                            Sign out of the enterprise IdP locally and clear EMA-minted server tokens (prints the IdP end-session URL when available)
  tools/list [options]                                       MCP tools/list against the current connection
  tools/call [options] [toolName] [toolArgs...]              MCP tools/call against the current connection
  resources/list [options]                                   MCP resources/list against the current connection
  resources/read [options] [uri]                             MCP resources/read against the current connection
  resources/templates/list [options]                         MCP resources/templates/list against the current connection
  resources/directory/read [options]                         MCP resources/directory/read against the current connection
  resources/subscribe [options] [uri]                        MCP resources/subscribe against the current connection
  resources/unsubscribe [options] [uri]                      MCP resources/unsubscribe against the current connection
  prompts/list [options]                                     MCP prompts/list against the current connection
  prompts/get [options] [promptName]                         MCP prompts/get against the current connection
  prompts/complete [options]                                 MCP prompts/complete against the current connection
  logging/setLevel [options] [level]                         MCP logging/setLevel against the current connection
  logging/tail [options]                                     MCP logging/tail against the current connection
  tasks/list [options]                                       MCP tasks/list against the current connection
  tasks/get [options] [taskId]                               MCP tasks/get against the current connection
  tasks/cancel [options] [taskId]                            MCP tasks/cancel against the current connection
  tasks/result [options] [taskId]                            MCP tasks/result against the current connection
  tasks/update [options] [taskId]                            MCP tasks/update against the current connection
  roots/list [options]                                       MCP roots/list against the current connection
  roots/set [options]                                        MCP roots/set against the current connection
  skills/list [options]                                      MCP skills/list against the current connection
  skills/get [options] [uri]                                 MCP skills/get against the current connection
  elicitation/respond [options] <elicitationId> [fields...]  Answer a pending server elicitation (from elicitationPending output): form answers as key:=value pairs / JSON, --done for URL mode, or --decline / --cancel
  daemon                                                     Daemon control
  private                                                    Print shell exports for a private daemon (eval "$(mcpdo private)"). Later mcpdo commands in that shell use an isolated, token-gated daemon.
  agent-help [options]                                       Print an agent-oriented usage guide, comparable to the mcpdo SKILL. Agents should read this before using other mcpdo commands.
  help [command]                                             Display help for command
